'''Owlbrow''' (まゆげどり, ''Mayu-ge Dori'') is a [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy that appears in [[The Aku Realms]] and [[Legend Stages]]. He was added in [[Version 2.0 Update|Version 2.0]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Owlbrow
|image = E 037.png
|first appearance = '''SoL''': [[The Wind Blows|Sub-chapter 9 - The Wind Blows]]<br>
'''Aku Realms''': [[Maldives (Aku Realm)|Maldives/Tokushima]]
|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[Pre-Fab Cathedral|Sub-chapter 14 - Pre-Fab Cathedral]]
|money drop = 800¢ - 3,160¢
}}

==Enemy==
Owlbrow is similar to [[Mooth]], but has a much lower money drop and hits much heavier in exchange for reduced attack rate and movement speed. His long backswing allows him to hide behind enemies that have a higher range than him, such as [[Li'l Eraser Cat (Enemy)|Li'l Eraser Cat]] in [[Tiny Will (Deadly)|Tiny Will]], because units tend to walk back into his range during his backswing, causing him to stay in place during the next attack. Fortunately, Owlbrow's health isn't too high for the threat he poses.

==Strategy==
The main threat posed by Owlbrow is the ability to obliterate close/mid-ranged attackers such as [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hip Hop Cat]], [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Swimmer Cat]], [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Mer-Cat]] and many crowd-controllers like [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Bishop Cat]] because they get outranged. Of course, this is not always the case, provided your levels.

Still, stalling him is pretty easy, and this allows attackers that outrange him to safely attack. The most effective counter to him in mid-game is easily [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Salon Cat]], since this enemy is often encountered in groups and protected by peons, but [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Lizard]]/[[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Lizard Cat]] or [[Archer Cat (Rare Cat)|Cataur]] could also be used to pick them off one by one. Another option is to snipe them using [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave]] or [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]] attackers like [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Gross Cat]] or [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Vaulter Cat]], as his health isn't very high and will eventually plummet over time.

Since Owlbrow has no idle animation, only backswing, the [[Cat Cannon]] is an easy way to synchronize groups of Owlbrows.

